  The PySCF Developers. All Rights Reserved.

The applicable upstream copyright years, authors, source paths and KAGAMI
modifications are retained in the affected files and LICENSES/PySCF.txt.
The full Apache-2.0 license is in LICENSE. Include these attribution files
when redistributing the affected source or binaries.

* src/posthf/mrpt/nevpt2.cpp -- the NEVPT2 active-space intermediate
  builders (make_rm2/make_rm3/make_hdm*/make_f3ca/make_f3ac and the
  make_a7..make_a25 Koopmans/auxiliary matrices) are derived from PySCF's
  pyscf/mrpt/nevpt2.py. MODIFICATIONS by the KAGAMI authors: translated from
  Python/NumPy to C++ and re-expressed against KAGAMI's storage/index
  conventions.

* src/scf/smd_sasa.cpp -- the electrostatic-cavity van der Waals fallback
  radii table (kElectrostaticFallbackRadii) reproduces the values in PySCF's
  pyscf.data.radii.VDW, whose primary source is the ASE / WebElements
  compilation of Bondi/Mantina-type van der Waals radii.

* src/dft/dft_grid.cpp -- the Bragg-Slater radii for K..Og used by the
  Lebedev level grids (extended_bragg_slater_radius_bohr) reproduce the values
  in PySCF's pyscf.data.radii.BRAGG, whose primary source is J. C. Slater,
  J. Chem. Phys. 41, 3199 (1964); the per-period radial point counts and
  Lebedev rule sizes of the grid levels follow the level tables of PySCF's
  pyscf.dft.gen_grid (RAD_GRIDS, ANG_ORDER), and the radius-dependent angular
  pruning follows the NWChem scheme as implemented there (nwchem_prune).

* src/posthf/cc/ccsd_engine.cpp -- RCCSD amplitude-update organization and
  OVVV intermediates adapted from pyscf/cc/ccsd.py to C++ storage and BLAS.

* src/posthf/cc/uccsd_blocked_engine.cpp -- the perturbative triples
  section follows pyscf/cc/uccsd_t_slow.py via the Python reference harness.

* src/posthf/cc/uccsd_blocked_lambda_rdm.cpp -- Lambda, density matrices
  and gradient assembly adapted from pyscf/cc/gccsd_lambda.py,
  gccsd_rdm.py, uccsd_rdm.py, uccsd_t_lambda.py and pyscf/grad/uccsd.py.
  src/posthf/cc/uccsd_gradient.cpp also adapts the latter gradient recipe.

* src/posthf/cc/uccsd_blocked_t_grad.cpp -- triples Lambda/density
  contributions adapted from pyscf/cc/uccsd_t_lambda.py and uccsd_t_rdm.py.
  KAGAMI changes include C++ spin-block storage, shared intermediates,
  derivative-integral/response interfaces and low-memory pair slabs.

* scripts/uccsd_spin_integrated_ref/{lambda_check,triples_check,
  gamma2_grad_check,t_grad_check,t_grad_lowmem_check}.py -- adapted PySCF
  routines and their spin-block/low-memory variants, with KAGAMI's numerical
  verification harness. These files are included adaptations, even though
  they are development tools rather than runtime dependencies.

A comparison with PySCF outputs does not, by itself, establish whether an
implementation is independent. See LICENSES/PySCF.txt for the per-file map.

The Lebedev-Laikov angular quadrature tables in src/scf/lebedev.cpp (21
rules, 6 to 1454 points) are from D. Laikov's public-domain distribution.

