Third-party data included in this repository
============================================================================

* data/basis/*.json -- Gaussian basis set definitions obtained from the
  Basis Set Exchange (https://www.basissetexchange.org, MolSSI) through its
  REST API and converted to KAGAMI's JSON layout by tools/import_bse.py.
  The 31 unmodified BSE responses, including per-element literature
  references, are kept in data/basis/_source/. Their element records were
  checked against the corresponding basis versions in BSE 0.12.
  The upstream collection is distributed under BSD-3-Clause; its copyright
  notice, conditions and disclaimer are reproduced in data/basis/LICENSE:
    Copyright (c) 2020 The Molecular Sciences Software Institute, Virginia Tech
    https://github.com/MolSSI-BSE/basis_set_exchange/blob/v0.12/LICENSE
  Preserve that file with redistributed raw or converted BSE material.
  No separate CC-BY-4.0 license for these files has been established.
  data/basis/ecp-test.json is a KAGAMI-authored synthetic test fixture
  (Apache-2.0), not BSE material. Citation for BSE: B. P. Pritchard,
  D. Altarawy, B. Didier,
  T. D. Gibson, T. L. Windus, J. Chem. Inf. Model. 59, 4814 (2019).

* src/dft/dispersion_d3_data.inc and src/dft/dispersion_d4_data.inc --
  DFT-D3(BJ) and DFT-D4 reference data (reference coordination numbers,
  reference C6 coefficients, reference dynamic polarizabilities, EEQ
  parameters, covalent radii, <r4>/<r2> expectation values, ...).  Both
  files are generated by tools/gen_dispersion_data.py from the Grimme
  group's own Apache-2.0 distributions of these data, fetched from pinned
  commits:
    tad-dftd3        https://github.com/dftd3/tad-dftd3           (Apache-2.0)
    tad-dftd4        https://github.com/dftd4/tad-dftd4           (Apache-2.0)
    tad-multicharge  https://github.com/grimme-lab/tad-multicharge (Apache-2.0)
    tad-mctc         https://github.com/grimme-lab/tad-mctc        (Apache-2.0)
  Copyright (C) Grimme Group.  The per-functional D3(BJ) and D4(BJ)-ATM
  damping parameters in src/dft/dispersion.cpp match the d3.toml / d4.toml
  tables distributed with tad-dftd4.  Primary literature: S. Grimme,
  J. Antony, S. Ehrlich, H. Krieg, J. Chem. Phys. 132, 154104 (2010);
  S. Grimme, S. Ehrlich, L. Goerigk, J. Comput. Chem. 32, 1456 (2011);
  E. Caldeweyher, C. Bannwarth, S. Grimme, J. Chem. Phys. 147, 034112
  (2017); E. Caldeweyher et al., J. Chem. Phys. 150, 154122 (2019);
  covalent radii from P. Pyykko, M. Atsumi, Chem. Eur. J. 15, 186 (2009).
  No material from the LGPL-licensed simple-dftd3 or dftd4 programs is
  included.

Other bundled numerical tables (SMD and PCM radii, standard atomic masses
and isotopic masses, the covalent radii used by the GUI) are values taken
from the published literature cited in the source comments and in
docs/01_basics/libraries_and_data.html.  The FMO hybrid-orbital
projection tables in src/scf/fmo_projection.cpp and the molecule-builder
fragment library in tools/kagami_gui/fragments/library.json were computed
by the KAGAMI authors (see tools/gen_fmo_hmo_from_methane.py and
tools/generate_builder_templates.py).

